e game. The engine's choice was G3. White took G3 next and sealed off the right side of the bottom."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "C2 was the 20k's biggest slip at 6.6 points, but it only moved the lead from -23.7 to -17.1. With Black so far behind, the slip hardly mattered and White still held a big margin."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The `inspect` code stored in command 4 (functions `parse`, `topo`, `audit`) only parses the board text, computes chains, liberties and empty regions, and checks the effect of the one move the player named, while later commands persist records, replay the finished game, and write the SGF and review files. No code loops over candidate moves, scores points, or plays out continuations, so nothing chose or ranked moves.", "stop": false}}